{#
  A campaign whose copy lives in a database row.

  ── THIS FILE IS THE SKELETON, AND THE SKELETON IS NOT EDITABLE ────────────

  Everything structural here was proved by `templates/emails/final-hours.twig` and is
  held by EmailInboxCompatTest: the fluid-hybrid wrapper that survives Gmail stripping
  <style>, the MSO conditionals, the VML button, the styled alt text on the countdown,
  role="presentation" on every layout table, the hidden preheader, no data: URIs, and
  no CSP nonce. An operator editing copy cannot reach any of it.

  What they edit is an ordered list of TYPED BLOCKS, rendered below. Each block's text
  arrives as plain text — EmailCampaign::clean() strip_tags everything on the way in —
  and this file supplies the markup. There is deliberately no block type that emits raw
  HTML: a rich-text editor emits <div>s and inline styles Outlook drops on the floor,
  which is the whole reason this design exists rather than a WYSIWYG.

  Links are resolved before they arrive. A block names its destination by KEY
  (vote_url, events_url, site_url) and EmailCampaign::resolve() turns it into this
  recipient's URL, so a campaign cannot carry a typed-in link, and vote_url can differ
  per person.

  Rendered once per recipient, so autoescaping applies to every name that lands here —
  a nominee called "Ade & Sons" must not break the markup around them.

  ── REBUILT 3 OCT 2026: THE HANDOFF'S LADDER, AND ACCENT'S COLOURS ──────────

  Deleted and written again from docs/handoff/inventory/_emails.md (owner, 3 Oct 2026).
  Type sits on REFERENCE §6.2's closed ladder — the 10px and 11px labels are 11.5, and
  nothing is smaller but the 1px preheader collapse, which is a hiding device and not
  type (TypeScaleTest). px is right here: no Display & reading setting reaches an inbox,
  and rem is ignored by enough clients to be a gamble. Every colour is `c.<token>`,
  `Accent::mail()` passed in by the sender under the handoff's own names — mail cannot
  read `var()`, but it need not type a palette of its own either, and this file used to
  type thirty-odd colours that were in no palette at all. The dark-mode block is ink as
  the ground and ground as the words, as the newsletter's always was: the handoff names
  no dark palette, so none is invented. The mono and capitals rules are for screens
  (MonoAndCaseTest leaves mail out), so the tracked micro-labels keep their voice.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
<meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no, date=no, address=no, email=no, url=no">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
<title>{{ subject }}</title>
<!--[if mso]>
<noscript>
<xml>
<o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
<o:PixelsPerInch>96</o:PixelsPerInch>
</o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
</xml>
</noscript>
<![endif]-->
<style>
  body, table, td, a { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
  table, td { mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; }
  img { -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; border: 0; height: auto; line-height: 100%; outline: none; text-decoration: none; display: block; }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 0; width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; background-color: {{ c.ground }}; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse !important; }
  a[x-apple-data-detectors] { color: inherit !important; text-decoration: none !important; font-size: inherit !important; font-family: inherit !important; font-weight: inherit !important; line-height: inherit !important; }
  u + #body a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  #MessageViewBody a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  span.MsoHyperlink { color: inherit; mso-style-priority: 99; }
  [data-ogsc] .agw-bg { background-color: {{ c.surface }} !important; }
  [data-ogsc] .agw-text { color: {{ c.ink }} !important; }

  /* Outlook (Word engine) ignores line-height unless told the rule is exact, and
     collapses to single spacing on long paragraphs. */
  p, td, a, div, h1 { mso-line-height-rule: exactly; }

  /* ── DARK MODE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     `color-scheme: light` above already stops Apple Mail and iOS inverting anything,
     which is why the palette below is a deliberate dark counterpart rather than a
     defensive one — Accent's ink as the ground and its ground as the words, because
     the handoff names no dark palette and this file will not invent one. Gmail's and Outlook.com's dark modes invert regardless and do it
     badly on near-white surfaces — dark text left on a darkened background. Declaring
     the dark values explicitly means the clients that DO honour the query render a
     chosen design, and the ones that force-invert have less to get wrong. */
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .agw-body   { background-color: {{ c.ink }} !important; }
    .agw-bg     { background-color: {{ c.ink }} !important; }
    .agw-text   { color: {{ c.ground }} !important; }
    .agw-muted  { color: {{ c.line }} !important; }
    .agw-body-t { color: {{ c.tint }} !important; }
    .agw-hero   { background-color: {{ c['ink-2'] }} !important; }
    .agw-rule   { border-color: {{ c['ink-2'] }} !important; }
    /* The green CTA already clears 4.5:1 against white text, so it is left alone —
       lightening it here would only reduce that. */
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 600px) {
    .agw-wrapper { width: 100% !important; }
    .agw-px { padding-left: 28px !important; padding-right: 28px !important; }
    .agw-headline { font-size: 26px !important; line-height: 32px !important; }
    .agw-btn-pad { padding-left: 28px !important; padding-right: 28px !important; }
    .agw-hero-pad { padding: 28px 20px !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body id="body" class="agw-body" style="margin:0; padding:0; background-color:{{ c.ground }};">

{# The brand mark is a HOSTED PNG, not an inlined data: URI.

   It was base64 — 20,848 bytes, over half the entire email — and Gmail, Outlook desktop,
   Outlook.com and Yahoo all refuse data: URIs in an img src, so the majority of readers
   paid that weight and saw the alt text anyway. It also spent half the headroom before
   Gmail's ~102KB clipping point, and what Gmail clips off a campaign is the footer, which
   is where the unsubscribe link lives.

   Not the SVG at /assets/img/logo-africa-gates.svg either: it is 1.4MB of embedded
   bitmap, and email clients do not render SVG at all. #}
<!-- PREHEADER -->
<div style="display:none; max-height:0; overflow:hidden; mso-hide:all; font-size:1px; line-height:1px; color:{{ c.ground }}; opacity:0;">
  {{ preheader ?: 'Voting closes soon. Rally your supporters and get them a seat.' }}
  &nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;
</div>

<table role="presentation" class="agw-body" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="{{ c.ground }}" style="background-color:{{ c.ground }};">
<tr>
<td align="center" style="padding:32px 12px;">


  <!--[if mso]>
  <table role="presentation" width="560" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:560px;"><tr><td>
  <![endif]-->
  {# FLUID-HYBRID, not a fixed 560px table.

     This was width="560" with the mobile override living only inside the one @media
     block. Gmail strips <style> in several configurations (notably a non-Gmail address
     fetched via POP/IMAP into a Gmail account), and when it does, a 560px table lands on
     a 320px screen: the reader gets a horizontally scrolling email or a zoomed-out one.
     A percentage width with a max-width needs no media query to work, and the MSO
     conditional above gives Outlook — which ignores max-width — its fixed 560. #}
  <table role="presentation" class="agw-wrapper agw-bg" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:100%; max-width:560px; background-color:{{ c.surface }}; border-radius:20px; overflow:hidden;">

    <!-- DARK HEADER BAR (logo left, status badge right) -->
    <tr>
      <td style="background-color:{{ c.ink }};">
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
          <tr>
            <td class="agw-px" style="padding:20px 32px;">
              <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
                <tr>
                  <td valign="middle">
                    <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
                      <tr>
                        <td valign="middle" width="40" style="padding-right:10px;">
                          {# THE MARK ONLY, not the full lockup. The wordmark version is
                             illegible below about 96px, and the words "Africa GATES" are
                             already set in live text in the cell beside this one — printing
                             them twice, once as unreadable pixels, is worse than not
                             printing them at all.

                             Served at 2x (192px for a 40px box) so it is not soft on a
                             retina phone, which is where most of these are opened. #}
                          <img src="{{ site_url }}/assets/img/logo-mark.png" width="40" height="40" alt="Africa GATES" style="display:block;">
                        </td>
                        <td valign="middle">
                          <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.surface }}; line-height:16px;">Africa</p>
                          <p style="margin:1px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:2px; color:{{ c['green-light'] }}; line-height:14px;">GATES</p>
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                    </table>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="middle" align="right">
                    <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:1.6px; color:{{ c.line }}; text-transform:uppercase;">Final Hours</p>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <!-- HERO: live countdown GIF -->
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-hero-pad agw-hero" align="center" bgcolor="{{ c['green-wash'] }}" style="background-color:{{ c['green-wash'] }}; padding:40px 20px;">
        <!-- Animated GIF, redrawn by the server on every open, so the time is true each
             time the message is looked at rather than true when it was sent. Frame 1 is a
             correct still for Outlook, which never advances past it. -->
        {# IMAGES OFF IS THE COMMON CASE, NOT THE EDGE CASE. Outlook desktop blocks remote
           images by default and so does most corporate mail. The countdown IS the hero, so
           with images off this block has to still carry the deadline:

             · the alt text is STYLED — an unstyled alt renders as 10px browser-default
               serif and reads as a broken attachment rather than as words somebody wrote;
             · width/height are set so a blocked image reserves its box instead of
               collapsing the panel to nothing;
             · the deadline is repeated as real text underneath, which is the line that
               actually does the work when the image never arrives. #}
        <img src="{{ countdown_url }}" width="320" height="104" alt="{{ countdown_alt }}"
             style="display:block; width:100%; max-width:320px; height:auto; margin:0 auto;
                    font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-weight:700;
                    line-height:1.4; color:{{ c.ink }}; text-align:center;">
        <p class="agw-muted" style="margin:16px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c['ink-2'] }}; mso-line-height-rule:exactly; line-height:18px;">Voting closes {{ closes_human }}</p>
      </td>
    </tr>

    {# ── THE EDITABLE PART ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
       One table row per block, in the order the operator arranged them. Each arm
       below is the markup the shipped "final hours" campaign used for that shape,
       so a campaign built from the starter blocks renders identically to the file
       it replaced — that was the acceptance test for this whole change.

       `first` is used only to give the top block the larger padding the headline
       had, so a campaign that does not open with a headline does not start flush
       against the countdown. #}
    {% for b in blocks %}
      {% set first = loop.first %}

      {% if b.type == 'hero' %}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px" align="center" style="padding:{{ first ? '36px' : '30px' }} 40px 0 40px;">
            {% if b.headline or b.accent %}
              <h1 class="agw-headline agw-text" style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight:700; font-size:28px; line-height:34px; color:{{ c.ink }}; letter-spacing:-0.3px; text-align:center;">
                {{ b.headline }}{% if b.accent %}{% if b.headline %} {% endif %}<span style="color:{{ c.green }};">{{ b.accent }}</span>{% endif %}
              </h1>
            {% endif %}
            {% if b.standfirst %}
              <p style="margin:10px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:{{ c.soft }}; text-align:center;">
                {{ b.standfirst }}
              </p>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
        </tr>

      {% elseif b.type == 'quote' %}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px" style="padding:{{ first ? '36px' : '32px' }} 40px 0 40px;">
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
              <tr>
                <td style="border-left:2px solid {{ c.green }}; padding:2px 0 2px 16px;">
                  <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:{{ c.soft }}; font-style:italic;">
                    "{{ b.text }}"{% if b.source %} &mdash; {{ b.source }}{% endif %}
                  </p>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
          </td>
        </tr>

      {% elseif b.type == 'paragraph' %}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px" style="padding:{{ first ? '36px' : '18px' }} 40px 0 40px;">
            {% for para in (b.paras ?? [b.text]) %}
              <p style="margin:0 0 {{ loop.last ? '0' : '12px' }} 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:23px; color:{{ c['ink-2'] }};">
                {{ para }}
              </p>
            {% endfor %}
          </td>
        </tr>

      {% elseif b.type == 'heading' %}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px" style="padding:{{ first ? '36px' : '34px' }} 40px 0 40px;">
            <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight:700; font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:1.2px; color:{{ c.soft }}; text-transform:uppercase;">
              {{ b.text }}
            </p>
          </td>
        </tr>

      {% elseif b.type == 'ask' %}
        {# The number is the count of ask blocks so far, not the loop index — a
           paragraph between two asks must not make them "01" and "03". #}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px" style="padding:18px 40px 0 40px;">
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
              <tr>
                <td width="30" valign="top" style="padding:1px 14px 0 0;">
                  <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.green }};">{{ b.n }}</p>
                </td>
                <td valign="top">
                  {% if b.title %}
                    <p style="margin:0 0 3px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:21px; color:{{ c.ink }}; font-weight:700;">
                      {{ b.title }}
                    </p>
                  {% endif %}
                  {% if b.text %}
                    <p style="margin:0 0 8px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:21px; color:{{ c.soft }};">
                      {{ b.text }}
                    </p>
                  {% endif %}
                  {% if b.link_label %}
                    <a href="{{ b.href }}" target="_blank" style="font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.green }}; text-decoration:none;">
                      {{ b.link_label }} &nbsp;&rarr;
                    </a>
                  {% endif %}
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
          </td>
        </tr>

      {% elseif b.type == 'callout' %}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px" style="padding:32px 40px 0 40px;">
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color:{{ c.ink }}; border-radius:14px;">
              <tr>
                <td align="center" style="padding:26px 28px;">
                  {% for para in (b.paras ?? [b.text]) %}
                    <p style="margin:0 0 {{ loop.last ? '0' : '10px' }} 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:23px; color:{{ c.surface }};">
                      {{ para }}
                    </p>
                  {% endfor %}
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
          </td>
        </tr>

      {% elseif b.type == 'button' %}
        {# Both halves are required and EmailInboxCompatTest checks for each: the VML
           roundrect is the only button Outlook's Word engine will render, and
           <w:anchorlock/> stops it being draggable. #}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px agw-btn-pad" align="center" style="padding:32px 40px 0 40px;">
            <!--[if mso]>
            <v:roundrect xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" href="{{ b.href }}" style="height:48px;v-text-anchor:middle;width:300px;" arcsize="12%" strokecolor="{{ c.green }}" fillcolor="{{ c.green }}">
            <w:anchorlock/>
            <center style="color:{{ c.surface }};font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;">{{ b.label }}</center>
            </v:roundrect>
            <![endif]-->
            <!--[if !mso]><!-->
            <a href="{{ b.href }}" target="_blank" style="display:inline-block; width:100%; max-width:300px; box-sizing:border-box; background-color:{{ c.green }}; border-radius:8px; padding:15px 24px; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.surface }}; text-decoration:none; text-align:center;">
              {{ b.label }}
            </a>
            <!--<![endif]-->
          </td>
        </tr>
        {% if b.secondary_label %}
          <tr>
            <td align="center" style="padding:14px 40px 0 40px;">
              <a href="{{ b.secondary_link_href }}" target="_blank" style="font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c['ink-2'] }}; text-decoration:underline;">
                {{ b.secondary_label }}
              </a>
            </td>
          </tr>
        {% endif %}

      {% elseif b.type == 'signoff' %}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px" style="padding:38px 40px 0 40px;">
            {% for para in (b.paras ?? [b.text]) %}
              {% if para %}
                <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:{{ c.soft }};">
                  {{ para }}
                </p>
              {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
            {% if b.salutation %}
              <p style="margin:0 0 2px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:{{ c.soft }};">{{ b.salutation }}</p>
            {% endif %}
            {% if b.signature %}
              <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight:700; font-size:14px; color:{{ c.ink }};">{{ b.signature }}</p>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
        </tr>

      {% elseif b.type == 'divider' %}
        <tr>
          <td class="agw-px" style="padding:28px 40px 0 40px;">
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
              <tr><td style="border-top:1px solid {{ c.line }}; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
            </table>
          </td>
        </tr>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}

    <!-- FOOTER -->
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-px" align="center" style="padding:36px 40px 32px 40px;">
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
          <tr><td style="border-top:1px solid {{ c['line-3'] }}; font-size:0; line-height:0; padding-bottom:22px;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:1.2px; color:{{ c.green }}; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase;">Africa G.A.T.E.S.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 14px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; color:{{ c.soft }};">
          {{ postal_address }}
        </p>
        <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; color:{{ c.soft }};">
          <a href="{{ site_url }}" style="color:{{ c.soft }}; text-decoration:underline;">africagates.org</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color:{{ c.soft }}; text-decoration:underline;">Unsubscribe</a>
        </p>
      </td>
    </tr>

  </table>
  <!--[if mso]>
  </td></tr></table>
  <![endif]-->

</td>
</tr>
</table>

</body>
</html>
